    why: "UC-ONBOARD needed no amendment. The plan expected one; it was read and found unnecessary - UC-ONBOARD is a contract about capability and truthfulness, and run #8 changed layout. Every promise survives verbatim: the disclosure still auto-opens on failure, status is still probe-or-capture and never the stepper cursor, only a decrypted flow reveals the list. Recorded rather than edited - a cosmetic amendment to close a checklist item would be worse than leaving a true document alone"
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-13-onboarding-capabilities.html
    why: "No amendment, and one question owed, recorded in both the coverage map and the result. Run #8 lists unset-the-proxy as deliberately unused on the grounds it belongs to a settings surface, but the affordance ships inside the set-proxy step of this very screen, so the premise is false about where it lives. DEC-13 names symmetric revert as part of why the app may write OS state. The assertion is capability-bound and stands until the owner decides; a design run may not narrow a shipped capability by listing it unused"
